Z||000000||Homicidal||05-04-2000||01:53 AM||||Okay:<P>I started my car recently and I notice hesitation, just a SLIGHT bit, and a bit low revs.  Just about 1/2 hour ago I started the car and it dies two times before idling and staying alive.  ?????<P>As if that wasn't confusing enough, my music on my cd changer cuts out randomly, not a lot, but it did it two times when driving to the store!  It just cuts out for around 5 seconds and then comes back.  Are both of these due to maybe a slightly dead battery?<P>I did wash my car 2 days ago and left the radio + 250W amplifier going for around 1-2 hours straight.  Could this have drained it some?<P>Other than that, I can't think of what would cause the car to stutter/not start PLUS the music cutting out also besides an electrical problem.  Any suggestions?<P>P.S. I am using a battery charger as we speak, just in case it IS the battery!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Homicidal||05-04-2000||02:21 AM||||UPDATE:<P>I tried it once more, with my dad watching.<P>This time is had a REALLY hard time getting started, sputtering and all until I gave it some gas.  My dad said he saw a lot of black smoke coming out the exhaust.  Went I finally cut the engine we smelled an intense gas smell.<P>So I figure it's either:<P>a)Spark plugs <P>b)Spark Plug wires<P>c)Distributor cap knobs<P>d)Dirty carberator(sp?)<P>Am I probably right?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Greg Piet||05-04-2000||06:05 AM||||Did you wash the motor?<BR>Im thinking water in the distributor as an easy fix.<P>A common reason why flooding is the coolant temp sensor, or you got the MAP breather hole wet and screwed it up.  There is a tech warning post here about getting your MAP wet.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Homicidal||05-04-2000||10:08 AM||||No, but water COULD have gotten into the engine.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||05-04-2000||10:36 AM||||Inspect your distibutor cap, it don't take much moisture to make it miss. Check your plug wires too. Unless your car's been switched by someone, it has fuel injection, not a carb. You also might want to see if you can pull any trouble codes from the ECM. ||||reg||1
